---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ModeChange from '../components/mode-change.astro';
import FlipCard from '../components/FlipCard.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Why Software Development — Teodora Piel"
  description="Why I moved from chemistry into software development, and what I'm building along the way."
>
  <!-- Section 1: intro -->
  <div class="relative bg-[#ffffff] dark:bg-[#000000]">
	<!-- shared centered column -->
	<div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-5xl px-6 md:px-10 pt-16 pb-16">

		<!-- top bar: Home on the left, mode switch on the right -->
		<div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4">
			<a
				href="/"
				class="inline-block whitespace-nowrap px-[1.3em] py-[0.4em] text-[23px]
					border border-black text-black
					dark:border-[#cccccc] dark:text-white
					hover:text-[#ab3c00] dark:hover:text-[#7d7d7d] dark:hover:border-[#aaaaaa]
					hover:scale-110 transition-transform">
				Home
			</a>
			<ModeChange />
		</div>

		<h1 class="mt-12 text-[23px] text-left text-[#222222] dark:text-[#cccccc]">
			This is meant to give you a glimpse into my mind, my thoughts and my decisions.
			Click on the cards to learn more.
		</h1>
	</div>
  </div>

  <!-- Section 2: cards -->
  <div class="relative bg-[#fff4e6] dark:bg-[#222222] pt-16 pb-24">
	<h2 class="mx-auto w-full max-w-5xl px-6 md:px-10 font-sans text-[35px] text-[#160066] dark:text-[#ffffff]">
		Thoughts and Reasoning
	</h2>

	<div class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-x-5 gap-y-10 max-w-[860px] mx-auto pt-16 px-4">

		<div class="w-full max-w-[400px] relative z-[70] transition-all duration-200 hover:z-[100] md:hover:scale-[1.05]">
			<FlipCard title="Pursuit of Software Development"
				color="#FFF0DB" darkColor="#282224" darkTitleColor="#ffffff"
				size="w-full max-w-[400px] h-[880px] min-[380px]:h-[780px] min-[440px]:h-[600px]">
				<div slot="back">
					<div class="space-y-4">
						<p>
							I've wanted to learn coding for a long time, and during my master's program I finally seized
							the chance to dive in properly.
						</p>

						<p>
							Programming turned out to be a mix of logic and creativity. It makes it possible to tackle complex problems and watch the solution
							take shape piece by piece. This is what makes programming addictive. That's what made the decision simple: finish my
							degree in Chemistry, learn as much as I could along the way, and then move into
							software development. My master's thesis surprised me by bringing both worlds together, and I came out of it stronger in each.
						</p>

						<p>
							I'm early in that transition and still learning every day. Right now I'm looking for a
							role where I can keep building in a professional environment.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</FlipCard>
		</div>

		<div class="w-full max-w-[400px] relative z-[40] transition-all duration-200 hover:z-[100] md:hover:scale-[1.05]">
			<FlipCard title="Projects, Skills and Ideas"
				color="#FFF0DB" darkColor="#3B3131" darkTitleColor="#ffffff"
				size="w-full max-w-[400px] h-[880px] min-[380px]:h-[780px] min-[440px]:h-[600px]">
				<div slot="back">
					<div class="space-y-4">
						<p>
							During my time at university, I've worked on a number of projects. Some of those projects were part
							of my studies, others personal.
						</p>

						<p>
							I've used Python for data analysis and for automating
							workflows during my studies, including supervised learning and plugin development.
						</p>

						<p>
							My personal projects include this website, built with Astro and Tailwind CSS, and
							a small browser game in TypeScript. I've since decided that idea wasn't up to par,
							so I'm starting over with a new one.
						</p>

						<p>
							For now I'm only scratching the surface of what programming can do, but I'm excited
							to keep learning, find new challenges, and improve my skills.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</FlipCard>
		</div>

	</div>
  </div>
</Layout>